# Copy to .env (git-ignored) or export these in your pipeline.
#
# These describe a DEPLOYMENT, not a connector: which roles may query it, and where it goes. What a
# connector *is* — its handler class, its jar, its columns — lives in its own CDK stack, committed.
#
# Precedence: exported environment variables beat this file, and a connector's own
# <id>/cdk/.env beats this one. So a pipeline always wins, and one connector can override the rest.

# ── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two COA components reach a connector through Athena, as different roles. Each is granted
# lambda:InvokeFunction on the function, s3:GetObject under its spill prefix, and kms:Decrypt on its
# spill key. Comma-separate either variable to serve more than one COA deployment; set both to the
# same value if one role does both jobs.
#
#   serve     - runs the queries.
#   discovery - runs DESCRIBE, which is how the @pk / @fk constraint tags are read at all. Omit it
#               and the connector answers SELECT perfectly while no declared key is ever found.
#
# Read both from SSM in COA's own account, where they are authoritative — the role names are
# generated, so do not try to guess them:
#   aws ssm get-parameter --name /{prefix}/serve/runtime-role-arn        --query Parameter.Value
#   aws ssm get-parameter --name /{prefix}/sources/db-connector-role-arn --query Parameter.Value
#
# Pasted here rather than read by the connector on purpose: a connector normally runs in a different
# account from COA, and SSM parameters are not readable across accounts.
SERVE_ROLE_ARN=arn:aws:iam::111122223333:role/<the value of that SSM parameter>
DISCOVERY_ROLE_ARN=arn:aws:iam::111122223333:role/<the value of that SSM parameter>

# The connector's target region. EXPORT IT IN YOUR SHELL — a value here is ignored whenever you
# deploy through the CDK CLI, which sets CDK_DEFAULT_REGION from the active profile on every run,
# and that wins. Left here commented as documentation only.
#
#   AWS_REGION=<region> pnpm run deploy
#
# Deploying into the wrong region succeeds and leaves a connector nothing will ever query, so check
# the region in the synth output before you deploy.
# AWS_REGION=eu-central-1

# ── Optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Target account. Left unset, CDK resolves it from the active AWS profile and the stack becomes
# environment-agnostic. CDK_DEFAULT_ACCOUNT wins over this.
# AWS_ACCOUNT_ID=111122223333

# Prefixes the Lambda and stack names, for telling two deployments of the same connector apart when
# they share an account — two COA environments, or two instances of one source. Permissions do not
# depend on it: COA scopes invoke on the coa:connector tag, not on the function's name.
# FUNCTION_NAME_PREFIX=acme-dev-

# Example connector only: size its bulk_rows fixture past Athena's 6 MB response limit to exercise
# the S3 spill path. Both default small, so nothing spills unless you ask.
# EXAMPLE_BULK_ROWS=4096
# EXAMPLE_BULK_ROW_BYTES=2048
